ou think of 7? Is 7 a prime number? \u003cem\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u0026quot;Yes, 7 is a prime number.\u0026quot;\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/em\u003e Since 7 has only 2 factors i.e. 1 and 7, it is a prime number. Let\u0026#39;s study this in detail.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\r\n\u003cul\u003e\r\n\t\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eIs 7 a prime number? -\u003c/strong\u003e Yes\u003c/li\u003e\r\n\t\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eIs 7 a composite number? -\u003c/strong\u003e No\u003c/li\u003e\r\n\t\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ePrime Factors of 7 -\u003c/strong\u003e 7\u003c/li\u003e\r\n\t\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eIs 7 a perfect square? -\u003c/strong\u003e No\u003c/li\u003e\r\n\t\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFactors of 7 -\u003c/strong\u003e 1, 7\u003c/li\u003e\r\n\u003c/ul\u003e\r\n\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg alt=\"Is 7 a Prime Number?\" src=\"https://wmznlejcfq.s3-ap-southeast-1.amazonaws.com/media/prime-number/is-7-a-prime-number.png\" style=\"width:300px;\" /\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\r\n\u003ch2\u003eIs 7 a Prime Number?\u003c/h2\u003e\r\n\r\n\u003cp\u003eYes, 7 is a prime number. The number 7 is divisible only by 1 and the number itself. For a number to be classified as a prime number, it should have exactly two factors. Since 7 has exactly two factors, i.e. 1 and 7, it is a \u003ca href=\"https://www.cuemath.com/numbers/prime-numbers/\"\u003eprime number\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg alt=\"Is 7 a Prime or Composite?\" src=\"https://wmznlejcfq.s3-ap-southeast-1.amazonaws.com/media/prime-number/is-7-a-prime-or-composite-number.png\" style=\"width:400px;\" /\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\r\n\u003ch2\u003eHow is 7 a Prime Number?\u003c/h2\u003e\r\n\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo understand whether 7 is prime or composite, it is important to find its \u003ca href=\"https://www.cuemath.com/numbers/factors/\"\u003efactors\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFactors of 7:\u003c/strong\u003e 1, 7\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\r\n\u003cp\u003eTherefore, we can say that 7 is a prime number since it has only 2 factors.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\r\n\u003cp\u003e☛ \u003ca href=\"https://www.cuemath.com/calculators/prime-number-calculator/\"\u003ePrime Number Calculator\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\r\n\u003ch2\u003eIs 7 a Composite Number?\u003c/h2\u003e\r\n\r\n\u003cp\u003eNo, since 7 has only two factors, i.e. 1 and 7. In other words, 7 is not a \u003ca href=\"https://www.cuemath.com/numbers/composite-numbers/\"\u003ecomposite number\u003c/a\u003e because 7 doesn\u0026rsquo;t have more than 2 factors.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eProblem Statements: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\r\n\u003ctable border=\"1\"\u003e\r\n\t\u003ctbody\u003e\r\n\t\t\u003ctr\u003e\r\n\t\t\t\u003ctd\u003eIs 7 a Prime Number?\u003c/td\u003e\r\n\t\t\t\u003ctd\u003eYes\u003c/td\u003e\r\n\t\t\u003c/tr\u003e\r\n\t\t\u003ctr\u003e\r\n\t\t\t\u003ctd\u003eIs 7 a Composite Number?\u003c/td\u003e\r\n\t\t\t\u003ctd\u003eNo\u003c/td\u003e\r\n\t\t\u003c/tr\u003e\r\n\t\t\u003ctr\u003e\r\n\t\t\t\u003ctd\u003eIs 7 a Perfect Cube?\u003c/td\u003e\r\n\t\t\t\u003ctd\u003eNo\u003c/td\u003e\r\n\t\t\u003c/tr\u003e\r\n\t\t\u003ctr\u003e\r\n\t\t\t\u003ctd\u003eIs 7 a \u003ca href=\"https://www.cuemath.com/algebra/perfect-squares/\"\u003ePerfect Square\u003c/a\u003e?\u003c/td\u003e\r\n\t\t\t\u003ctd\u003eNo\u003c/td\u003e\r\n\t\t\u003c/tr\u003e\r\n\t\t\u003ctr\u003e\r\n\t\t\t\u003ctd\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://www.cuemath.com/algebra/cubes-and-cube-roots/\"\u003eCube Root\u003c/a\u003e of 7\u003c/td\u003e\r\n\t\t\t\u003ctd\u003e1.912930\u003c/td\u003e\r\n\t\t\u003c/tr\u003e\r\n\t\t\u003ctr\u003e\r\n\t\t\t\u003ctd\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://www.cuemath.com/numbers/multiples/\"\u003eMultiples\u003c/a\u003e of 7\u003c/td\u003e\r\n\t\t\t\u003ctd\u003e7, 14, 21, 28, 35, 42, 49, 56, 63, 70\u003c/td\u003e\r\n\t\t\u003c/tr\u003e\r\n\t\t\u003ctr\u003e\r\n\t\t\t\u003ctd\u003eIs 7 an \u003ca href=\"https://www.cuemath.com/numbers/even-numbers/